  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "Wall in the middle – one-two out of the corner and a one-timer from the far side",
  "description": "Half the court, goalkeeper in goal. Three lines: A with the balls in the corner next to the goal, B centrally a little out above the slot and C on the far side. A carries the ball a few metres up the boards and passes to B. B plays it straight back to A, who has moved to a new space. A plays a cross pass to C, who shoots first time. Straight after the pass, B heads in front of goal for the rebound.\n\nRotate A to B, B to C and C to A. Switch sides after a few minutes so everyone shoots from both sides.\n\nVariant: everything one touch – the passes and the shot. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "A: move after the pass so B gets a new, open passing angle."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "A: check on C before the ball comes back – is the shooter open?"
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Firm, flat passes along the floor, and the shot straight at goal."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "B: go to the net straight after the pass with the stick on the floor."
    }
  ],
